---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import SchemaMarkup from '../components/SchemaMarkup.astro';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from '../utils/schema';

const schema = [
  webPageSchema('Cookie Policy', 'eLan Technology cookie policy - types of cookies we use and how to manage them.', '/cookie-policy/'),
  breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Cookie Policy', url: '/cookie-policy/' }]),
];
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="eLan Technology cookie policy - types of cookies we use and how to manage them."
  lastUpdated="2026-09-24"
>
  <SchemaMarkup schema={schema} />

  <h2>What Are Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files that are placed on your device (computer, smartphone, or tablet)
    when you visit a website. They are widely used to make websites work efficiently and to provide
    information to the site owner. Cookies help us recognise your device on return visits and
    remember choices made on the website.
  </p>

  <h2>Types of Cookies We Use</h2>
  <p>We use the following categories of cookies on <a href="https://elan-tech.net">elan-tech.net</a>:</p>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6">
    <table class="min-w-full border border-[var(--border)] text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-[var(--bg-card)]">
        <tr>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 text-left font-semibold">Name / type</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 text-left font-semibold">Purpose</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 text-left font-semibold">Duration</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 text-left font-semibold">Required?</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 font-medium"><code>theme</code> (local storage)</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Remembers the visitor's light or dark display preference.</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Session or until you clear site storage</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Yes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 font-medium"><code>elan:privacy-consent</code> (local storage)</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Records the selected privacy categories, policy version and decision time. It does not contain a name, email address or advertising identifier.</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Until the visitor clears site storage or the consent version changes</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Yes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 font-medium"><code>lp-bar-ganesh-2026</code> (local storage)</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Remembers dismissal of the current campaign announcement.</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Until the visitor clears site storage</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Yes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 font-medium"><code>digibizid-slide-seen</code> (session storage)</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Prevents the same venture announcement from repeatedly appearing during one browser session.</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Browser session</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Yes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 font-medium"><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>, <code>_gid</code> and <code>_gat*</code></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Google Analytics audience and session measurement, delivered through Google Tag Manager.</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Varies by cookie; <code>_ga</code> may last up to two years</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">No - consent required</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2 font-medium"><code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code> and Microsoft-domain Clarity cookies</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Microsoft Clarity usage measurement and session analysis.</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">Varies by cookie and browser settings</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] px-4 py-2">No - consent required</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Third-Party Cookies</h2>
  <p>Some pages on our website include content from third-party services that may set their own cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager:</strong> used to understand website traffic and measure useful actions.
      Governed by the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Microsoft Clarity:</strong> used to understand how visitors use our pages.
      Governed by the <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Calendly:</strong> appointment scheduling on our consultation page. The Calendly script,
      embedded calendar and its third-party cookies remain blocked until you select “Load Calendly &amp;
      Choose a Time”. Calendly then processes the connection and booking under its own privacy and
      cookie terms. You may use our direct contact options without loading it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Razorpay:</strong> hosted payment options on our pricing and paid-audit sections. Razorpay remains blocked
      until you acknowledge the payment notice and select “Load secure payment options”. Razorpay
      may then use its own cookies or similar storage under its
      <a href="https://razorpay.com/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Optional analytics remain off unless you actively allow them. Google advertising storage,
    advertising-user data and advertising personalisation remain denied. We do not control the
    names or lifetimes of cookies set on third-party domains, so provider documentation should also
    be reviewed.
  </p>

  <h2>Managing Cookies</h2>
  <p>You have several options for managing cookies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Browser settings:</strong> most browsers allow you to block or delete cookies via
      Settings &gt; Privacy. Note that blocking essential cookies may affect site functionality.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Privacy &amp; cookie settings:</strong> use the control available in the website footer or the floating privacy button to accept, reject or withdraw optional analytics permission.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Rejecting analytics does not affect your ability to use the core features of our website.</p>

  <h2>Consent Record and Withdrawal</h2>
  <p>
    The website records only the selected analytics preference, consent-policy version and decision
    times in your browser’s local storage. It does not use that record as proof of identity. You can
    reopen “Privacy &amp; cookie settings” at any time and reject analytics. When optional analytics
    have already loaded, the website updates the consent state and reloads the page to stop further
    optional collection; provider cookies already stored may also be removed through browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookie Inventory Review</h2>
  <p>
    Cookie names and durations can change when a provider updates its software or when the website’s
    configuration changes. We review the deployed tags and this table when adding or materially
    changing a form, embed, analytics service, campaign tool or payment provider. Unknown optional
    tags should not be enabled until they have been classified and documented.
  </p>

  <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
  <p>
    We detect supported Global Privacy Control (GPC) and browser Do Not Track (DNT) signals and
    keep optional analytics off by default. The privacy interface remains available so you can make
    a separate, explicit choice for analytics on this website. Choosing analytics does not enable
    advertising storage, advertising-user data or advertising personalisation. You may withdraw the
    choice at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about our use of cookies, please contact us at:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@elan-tech.net">privacy@elan-tech.net</a></li>
    <li>
      Address: <a href="https://share.google/PklD3tFGBBqsPHjli" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">eLan Technology, Basement Floor, PTG IT Park, Plot No. 21, IT Park Rd, Gayatri Nagar, Nagpur, Maharashtra 440022, India</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
</LegalLayout>
